Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] xwayland: Show the window cursor for tablet tools

On proximity in, a tablet tool gets the seat's current X cursor, which
can be unset while the DIX considers the window's cursor shown. That
happens when the cursor became the sprite's cursor while the master
pointer had no xwl_seat yet, for example a window mapped under the
initial sprite position when Xwayland starts on demand and no device
has sent an event yet: xwl_set_cursor() ignores it, but miPointer marks
it as displayed. Later motion over windows with the same cursor then
changes nothing, so the tool keeps a hidden cursor until it crosses into
a window with a different one.

Invalidate the master's sprite on proximity in, as pointer enter does,
so the next tablet motion sets the cursor again.
---
 hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c
--- a/hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c
+++ b/hw/xwayland/xwayland-input.c
@@ -2170,6 +2170,8 @@ tablet_tool_proximity_in(void *data, struct zwp_tablet_tool_v2 *tool,
 
     xwl_tablet_tool->proximity_in_serial = serial;
     xwl_seat->tablet_focus_window = wl_surface_get_user_data(wl_surface);
+    if (xwl_tablet_tool->xdevice)
+        miPointerInvalidateSprite(GetMaster(xwl_tablet_tool->xdevice, POINTER_OR_FLOAT));
 
     /* If there is a cursor surface frame callback pending, we need to clear it
      * so that we can continue submitting new cursor frames.
